            0.111,
            0.561,
            0.885,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From perimeter, we move to area, i.e., to the ‘amount of space’ occupied by a two-dimensional region in a plane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.599,
            0.886,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measurement is always relative to something we call a unit. For area, the unit is a 1 × 1 square; its area is taken to be 1 unit"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (also written as 1 sq. unit). You know from Grade 8 that the area of a rectangle with sides a units and b units is ab sq. units (Fig. 6.16)."
            }
          ]
        },
